  "slug": "entangled-microwaves-nonlinear-scattering-ed74",
  "summary": "New preprints show moiré and hybrid-resonance control of polaritons, electron-phonon coupling and chiral phonons in graphene, plus THz flatbands.",
  "synthesis": "The items do not concern magnon microwave generation; the dominant thread is engineered hybrid excitations in graphene-based and related photonic systems. Several works treat moiré structure as a control knob: gate-tunable hyperbolic plasmon-phonon polaritons in twisted bilayer graphene, a Fano resonance from coupling between moiré flat-band electronic excitations and hBN out-of-plane optical phonons, and reconfigurable chiral phonons in asymmetrically stacked graphene moiré superlattices probed by helicity-resolved Raman spectroscopy. Complementary studies address hybrid plasmon-phonon eigenmodes with vortex states in a graphene ring on silica, and high-Q collective flatbands with zero group velocity in Mie-grating THz metasurfaces. What is new is the direct observation of moiré-induced interlayer electron-phonon coupling and the demonstration of tunability of polaritons, phonons and flatbands.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
